<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

	<ResearchProjectDef>
		<defName>RM_Replication</defName>
		<label>replication</label>
		<description>Splitting items into matter (mass and value), recording patterns and printing from them.\nUnlocks all replimat buildings.\nLiving printing (animals by DNA, people by templates) can be switched off in the mod settings: then the replimat prints only items and mechanoids.</description>
		<baseCost>1000</baseCost>
		<techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
		<prerequisites>
			<li>MicroelectronicsBasics</li>
			<li>Machining</li>
		</prerequisites>
		<researchViewX>11.00</researchViewX>
		<researchViewY>1.80</researchViewY>
		<discoveredLetterTitle>Replimat: how to build</discoveredLetterTitle>
		<discoveredLetterText>Replication researched: you can build the replimat.\nEverything goes on one power network.\n\nComputer: binds the operator's links to the replicators.\nA colonist with a replink, mechlink or biolink: right-click the computer, "Contact the computer".\nThis is done once, after that the operator is not needed at the computer.\nA bound link lets its group print, the link level sets the speed.\nIf the operator dies or leaves the map, printing stops.\n\nTank: stores matter: mass and value.\nLarge tank: the same, four times more matter.\nBuild as many tanks as you like.\n\nSplitter: like a crematorium, bills with filters.\nHaulers bring what fits, it is split into matter at once and its pattern is recorded.\nThe "Scan" button on an item sends one piece there.\n\nReplicator: like a workbench, bills are added in the replicator itself.\nIt prints from the tanks of its power network and puts the result nearby.\nWall replicator: the same, built into a wall.\nAnimal replicator: prints feed into itself, animals eat straight from it.\n\nBioscanner: records the DNA of an animal or a person for bioreplication.\nBioreplicator: prints adult tame animals by recorded DNA and colonists by templates.\nBioreplication can be switched off in the mod settings.</discoveredLetterText>
	</ResearchProjectDef>

